#
# The addon's entry point. The MAST runtime finds an addon by this file, and this file
# does nothing but declare what the addon offers and pull in its parts.
#
# `provides` names a capability other addons can depend on. Addons load in a
# NON-DETERMINISTIC order and share one global namespace, so "my addon uses a label from
# theirs" is only safe if it is declared:
#
#   requires <token>    HARD - the story fails to COMPILE if nothing provides it
#   suggests <token>    SOFT - a warning, and compilation continues
#
# Both are compile-time only, and both are v1.4.0 or later.
#
provides my_addon

import panel.mast
